{"id": "z0886", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is E, think. When someone sits quietly with their eyes moving, it often means they are daydreaming or processing thoughts internally. This kind of eye movement usually happens during mental activity rather than reading, which requires focused gaze on text. It might also be associated with meditation or falling asleep, but the most accurate choice here is thinking.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
