{"id": "z0910", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C: learn new things. People read non fiction to expand their knowledge, understand complex topics, and gain insights into the world around them.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z0918", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To grind wheat for bread, you need a mill. So the correct answer is E, mill.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z0926", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When a person admit s their mistakes, they are taking responsibility for what happened. Admitting errors means recognizing that one made a mistake and accepting the consequences or learning from it. It often involves acknowledging fault, which can lead to feeling relieved because it removes the need to deny or hide the issue. While some might feel grateful afterward, the primary action is being responsible. So the best answer is E, act responsibly.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z0934", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Making a schedule was easy to pick. The major called for knowledge that required a certain E, en cycloped ia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
