{"id": "z0998", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If they get a surprising show over and over again, it might start to feel annoying. At first, surprise can be fun, but if it keeps happening without any change or excitement, people could get irritated. So the best answer would be C, annoyance.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1006", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "John and Judy were parents with two light tough kids who weren' t always well-behaved. They felt it was a parent's job to guide children. So the answer is B, guide children.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1014", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When a person with mental illness receives medication and therapy, the most accurate outcome is that they have been effectively treated. The goal of these interventions is to manage symptoms, improve quality of life, and support recovery, rather than causing irrational behavior or suffering. While challenges may recur over time, effective treatment helps stabilize the condition.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1022", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Before nap time, a kinder garten teacher usually tells stories. This helps calm the kids down and get them ready to rest. So the answer is E: tell story.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1030", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, knowledge. If you're remembering something, it's because of your knowledge of it to begin with.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1038", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If he finds a bald eagle, the patriotic guy with the camera is most likely to photograph it. Bald eagles are a national symbol of the United States, so capturing their image would be a natural and meaningful thing for him to do.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1046", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "James told his son to settle down and be careful because there were many frogs mating in the area. Given that context, he likely didn ’t want his son to disturb them. So the best answer would be D: disturb.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1054", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, having a disability can make academic tasks difficult for someone because they might have trouble seeing or hearing, which makes it hard to follow lessons. Or maybe they move slower than others, so keeping up is tough. Sometimes their body doesn't work the same way as other people's, making it hard to write or use tools. They might also need more time to understand things, and that can be challenging in a classroom. So it’s not just about being smart; it ’s about how their body or mind works differently, which affects what they can do at school.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 35, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1062", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When we are running, what we're doing is moving quickly from one place to another. So the correct answer would be D: go quickly. We run because it's faster than walking or standing still. It helps us cover distance more efficiently and respond to things that need our attention.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1070", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To change their lives, people need to better themselves. While facing problems and paying bills are part of life, personal growth involves developing skills, building confidence, and making positive choices that lead to improvement. Becoming disillusioned or eating chicken doesn't directly contribute to transformation. So the best answer is B: better themselves.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1078", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "He was being a bit decept ive. While he wasn't flat out lying, leaving out key details means he was presenting an incomplete picture to influence how things were perceived. That makes him deceptive rather than just honest or imaginative.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1086", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If a person stutters when he experiences anxiety or excitement, he'll have difficult y express ing information. The stutter makes it hard to speak fluently during moments of stress, so getting his thoughts across can be challenging.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1094", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "While walking the student needed to store his writing instrument away, he put it in a desk drawer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1102", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If coffee sits in the fridge and loses its liquid form, that point is known as A. the freezing point. When the temperature drops low enough, the water content in the coffee turns into ice crystals. That' s why it becomes solid rather than just getting thicker or changing taste. The other options don't fit because there's no such thing as a prime point for liquids, the boiling point would mean it was heating up, and melting applies to turning from solid to liquid, not the reverse. So the correct answer is the freezing point.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1110", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A cooked lobster is a. inedible? No, that's not true. Cook ed lobsters are actually quite edible and popular in many places. B. see d? That doesn't make sense either. Lo bsters aren't seeds. C. dead? Well, when you cook a live lobster, it does die, so technically yes, it' s dead. But we eat them anyway. D. green? Not really. Cook ed lobsters turn more red or brown, not green.So the best answer is C, dead. Though we don' t mind eating them after they pass on!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1118", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, snake. Sn akes are known to be predator s because they hunt and eat other animals for food. Ants usually don't hunt large prey. Elephants are herbivores and graze on plants. Giraff es also eat plants, so they are not predator s either.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1126", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A. Su saphone is ancient. It's an old- fashioned type of telephone that used to be common before modern cell phones came along.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1134", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When creating music, the best choice is D: pl uck the strings of a fingerboard with your fingers. This directly relates to making sound on an instrument like a guitar or ukulele by using your fingers to create notes. The other options are not typically used for playing music; hitting a baseball bat or rattling a baby toy might make noise but aren't part of musical performance. Banging a wall could be loud but isn't intentional music-making. So, plucking string s with fingers is the correct answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1142", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The inside of a Thanksgiving turkey is white instead of pink because it' s cooked thoroughly, and the heat energy breaks down the my oglobin protein that gives meat its red color.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1150", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "An octopus protect s itself with D, pig ment squirting. They use their skin's ability to change color and pattern quickly to blend into surroundings or start le predators.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1158", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "None of these foods are inherently harmful to humans. However, conventional corn may contain higher levels of pesticides compared to organic options. So while all are edible, conventional corn might have a slightly greater exposure risk for some people due to chemical residue s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1166", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Roasting a turkey requires adding heat. That's what cook s the meat and browns the skin. So the correct answer is A, heat.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1174", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A. In verse. The amount of friction and the speed of an object have an inverse relationship. That means as one increase s, the other decrease s. For example, if there is more friction between two surfaces, it will be harder to move them quickly. Conversely, less friction allows objects to move faster with less resistance.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1182", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Thermometers are used to measure body temperature, so they can help you monitor a fever. They don't indicate levels of mercury in the blood or read exactly at 98.6 degrees, and they're not only for babies. So the correct answer is A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1190", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Asteroids crashing on planets can leave behind large bowl- shaped cavities in the ground. These impact craters form when a massive rock coll ides with the planet's surface at high speed, causing explosive force and material displacement. The resulting depression is typically bowl-shaped, often surrounded by raised rims of ejected debris.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1198", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A small creek absorb ing heat energy can result in the c reek water getting colder. When a stream absorb s heat, it uses that energy to warm up its own water, so if it's absorbing heat energy from the environment, like from the sun or surrounding air, it actually means the water temperature might drop slightly compared to what was there before. It doesn' t lead to a parched bed because absorption of heat usually relates to warming rather than drying out. Tri butaries branch off based on geography and terrain, not directly from he at absorption. And runoff is more about excess water moving off the land, which isn' t caused by heating. So the correct answer is that the creek water gets colder.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1206", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "DNA is a vehicle for passing closed types.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1214", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The light that appears dimm est is probably the star outside the window. Stars are incredibly distant, so even though they are very bright in their own right, by the time their light reaches us on Earth, it looks much faint er compared to lights closer by.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1222", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So if a UFO is flying overhead and it looks small then large, that would most likely mean the UFO is approaching. When something gets closer to you, it appears larger in size due to perspective. The change in apparent size suggests movement toward the observer rather than away or stationary changes like calling or being close already. Therefore, the correct answer is C, the UFO is approaching.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1230", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Wind can cause a, basement s to flood due to weather. When wind blows strongly, it can push rainwater or debris into basement s through cracks in the foundation, especially if there's heavy rain at the same time. The other options are not correct because small birds don't usually kill large birds, water falls flow downward due to gravity and cannot flow backward, and while stone s do weather down over time, wind isn' t typically the main cause; water and temperature changes are more significant factors.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1238", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The closest source of plasma to our planet is actually the cloud in the sky. While it might not be obvious, clouds are primarily composed of tiny water droplets or ice crystals, but they also contain trace amounts of ion s and charged particles due to various processes like radiation from solar wind interacting with atmospheric gases. This makes them a form of plasma at a very low density compared to stars or other celestial bodies.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1246", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The boy was able to warm the fireplace without a lighter thanks to friction. He probably used rubbing two objects together, like a stick and a piece of cloth, to create enough heat for sparks or ember s. This is a common way people have started fires in the past when they didn't have matches or lighters. So the answer is A, fri ction.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1254", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best soil for plants is usually option A, ma lable and nu tritious. This type of soil is easy to work with, holds moisture well, and provides the nutrients plants need to grow healthy. Dry and sandy soil drains too quickly and lacks nutrients. Grainy and bitter soil probably doesn't sound good for plant s either. Compact and hard soil makes it tough for roots to grow properly. So A is definitely the best choice.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1262", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If someone wants to start saving money for a nice vacation at the end of the year, they should look at their budget and find areas where they can cut back. Among the options given, quit ting eating lunch out is usually one of the most effective ways to save money. This can add up quickly since dining out often costs more than cooking at home or bringing lunch from home. Making more phone calls doesn' t really save money unless it replaces an expensive service like a restaurant reservation or taxi ride. Buying less with Mon opoly money isn't practical because Monop oly money isn't real cash. And having lunch with friends might actually cost more if you're sharing expenses. So, the best choice would be B, quit eating lunch out, as this directly reduces spending without cutting into other essential s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 45, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1270", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Grand Canyon was formed by the Colorado River. That river is named after the 38th state to join the Union, which is Colorado. So over time, as this river flow ed through the land, it car ved out the canyon. It wasn't a volcano or the Great Lakes dry ing up. It's the steady work of water cutting through rock over millions of years.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1278", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A, seeing a solar eclipse. That's the one that can cause people to crash their car. If you're looking at a so lar eclipse without proper eye protection, it could distract you and make you take your eyes off the road. The other options are good driving practices— using turn signals, following speed limits, and keeping your eyes on the road— all things that help prevent crashes. So the answer is definitely A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1286", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "December 2 1 through March 2 0 covers a three- month span, which typically aligns with winter in many parts of the world. This is an example of a season. The correct answer is C: season.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1294", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If you were attacked by a shark and had to punch it sharply where it pulls in air, you ’d use your hand to make contact with B. its gills. Sha rks breathe through their gills, which are located on the sides of their heads just behind the mouth. Pu nching there could disrupt their breathing and cause distress or disorient ation. While hitting other areas might hurt, targeting the gi l area would directly affect how the sha rk takes in oxygen.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
