{"id": "z1702", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So he's going to earn 21 dollars every week, and there are 21 6 weeks of harvest. That' s a lot of weeks. Let' s see how much money he earns in total first. We can multiply the amount he earns per week by the number of weeks. That would be 2 1 times 2 1 6. Now, if we do that calculation, we get 4 5 3 6 dollars earned during the whole season.But then he has to pay taxes, right? He has to give some of that money to the government. The problem says he has to pay 7 02 dollars in taxes. So let' s subtract that from his total earnings. If we take 4, 5 36 and subtract 7 02, that leaves him with 3,8 3 4 dollars. So after paying all his taxes, Lewis will have 3,8 34 dollars at the end of the harvest season.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 47, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1710", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So he has to give 32 pieces of junk mail to each block and gives 8 mails to each house. That means there are 4 houses in a block.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
