{"id": "z1726", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Rachel had five pages of math homework and two pages of reading homework. To find out how many more pages of math homework she had, you subtract the number of reading pages from the math pages: 5 minus 2 equal s 3. So, Ra chel had three more pages of math homework than reading homework.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1734", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the ring toss game made $1 44 each day, and they were at the carnival for 22 days. To find the total, you just multi ply the daily earnings by the number of days. That ’s 1 44 times 2 2. Let me do that quick calculation. 1 4 4 times 2 0 is 2,88 0, and 1 4 4 times 2 is 2 88. Add those together, and you get 3, 1 6 8. So, over 2 2 days, the ring toss game earned a total of $3, 1 6 8.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 42, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1742", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first chapter is 6 6 pages. The second chapter is 35 pages. And the third chapter is 2 4 pages. So, adding them up, 66 plus 3 5 is 101, and then 101 plus 2 4 is 1 25. So, the book has 1 25 pages altogether.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1750", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are seven large seat s on the ferris wheel. Each one can hold 12 people, so we just multiply those two numbers together to get our answer. Seven times twelve equals eighty four. So a total of eighty four people can ride the fer ris wheel in large seats.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1758", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 23, "onset_chunk": 22, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, if 7 05 visitors came that day and the previous two days had 1 9 1 and 4 57 visitors respectively, we can add those numbers to find out how many visited over those three days. So adding them up gives us a total of 1, 3 5 3 visitors. Now, to find out how many more visited on that specific day compared to all the other 2 4 5 days combined, we just need to subtract the visitors from those three days from the total number of visitors Rachel saw in those three days. So, 7 05 minus 1, 3 53 equal s negative 6 48. That means actually fewer people visited on that day than on the other 2 45 days combined. But since the question asks for how many more, it turns out there were no more visitors that day than on the rest; rather, fewer did visit.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 51, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1766", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Dan has $2 and wants to buy candy bars that cost $ 6 each. But wait, he only has $2, which is less than the price of one candy bar. So, unfortunately, he cannot buy any candy bars with the money he has. The answer is zero candy bars.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1774", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are six storks and two birds on the fence. When three more birds join, that makes five birds total. So there is one more stork than birds sitting on the fence.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
