{"id": "z1790", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "They have 14 chairs for each set of tables, and there are 9 sets. So they have 1 4 times 9, which is 12 6 chair s total. Since they have 9 sets of tables, that means they have 9 tables. To find out how many more chairs than table s they have, we subtract the number of tables from the number of chairs: 12 6 minus 9 equal s 1 17. So they have 1 17 more chairs than tables.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
