{"id": "z1814", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Marco and his dad picked 22 pounds together. Then on the way back, his dad found an extra 30 pounds of strawberries. Now Mar co's total is 3 6 pounds. That means his dad must have added those 3 0 pounds to what they had before. So originally, their combined weight was 22 pounds. If you add the 30 pounds his dad found, that makes 5 2 pounds in total for both of them now. Since Marco has 36 pounds, we subtract that from 52, which leaves his dad with 16 pounds of strawberries.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1822", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Winter is almost here, and most animals are migrating to warmer countries. There are 18 bird families living near the mountain. If 3 8 bird families flew away to Africa, and 80 bird families flew away to Asia, how many bird families flew away for the winter? First, we need to figure out how many bird families left in total. The ones that went to Africa were 38, and the ones that went to Asia were 80. So we add those together: 3 8 plus 8 0 equals 1 18. That means a total of 1 18 bird families flew away during the migration. So the answer is 1 1 8 bird families flew away for the winter.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 43, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1830", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "They have 1 1 sets of tables, and each set has 13 chairs. To find the total number of chairs, you multiply the number of sets by the number of chairs per set: 1 1 times 1 3. That equal s 1 4 3 chair s in total.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
