{"id": "z1846", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are two basket s, each with four red peaches and some green ones. So that means there are eight red peache s in total. If the total number of peache s is twelve, then the remaining four must be green peaches. Since these four green peaches are split between two basket s, there are two green peaches in each basket.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
