{"id": "z1862", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, if she lost 1 01 k g and she now weigh s 27 kg, then her original weight must have been the sum of these two amounts. So, 2 7 plus 1 01 equal s 1 28 k g. Therefore, before starting to jog, Jesse weighed 1 28 k g.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1870", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Lewis earns $3 6 8 every week during the harvest season, which last s for 59 weeks. He has to pay $3 88 in rent each week. To find out how much he pays as rent over the whole harvest period, we need to multi ply his weekly rent by the number of weeks. So that's 3 88 times 5 9. Let' s do the math: 3 88 multiplied by 5 9 equals 2 2 89 2 dollars. Therefore, Lewis pays a total of 2 2, 8 92 dollars in rent during the entire harvest season.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 38, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1878", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Paco had 4 0 cookies. He ate two, so he had 3 8 left. Then he bought 3 7 more. So 3 8 plus 3 7 is 75. So Pa co had 75 cookies in total.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1886", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Rachel had to complete 10 pages of math homework. Since she had to do 3 more pages of reading than math, that means she did 10 plus 3, which is 13 pages of reading. Add ing the math and reading together, 1 0 plus 13 equal s 23 pages in total. So, Ra chel had to complete 23 pages altogether.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1894", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If the machine made 9 shirts yesterday, and it can make 3 shirts per minute, then we divide the total number of shirts by the rate to find the time. So, 9 divided by 3 equal s 3. The machine worked for 3 minutes yesterday.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1902", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The GDP defl ator differs from the CPI in that it incorporates both current-year prices and base-year prices. While the CPI focuses on a fixed basket of consumer goods using current year prices, the GDP deflator measures the price level of all goods and services produced domestically, comparing current- year prices to those in a base year. This makes it broader but less precise for specific consumer trends compared to the CPI.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1910", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, the correct answer is B, solid slope. This fallacy occurs when someone assume s that because there's no evidence of harm or negative effects from a proposed change, it must therefore be safe or have no significant impact. It ignore s the possibility that an effect might exist even if we haven't observed it yet. The other options don't fit: poison ing the well involves dis crediting someone before they speak, appeal to tradition rely s on past practices without justification, and argument from authority uses someone' s status rather than evidence.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1918", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, we know that the photo electron spectrum will show peaks for electrons with different ion ization energies. The peak representing electrons with the lowest ionization energy would be the one most easily removed by photons. Looking at the elements given, neon is a noble gas with a full outer shell, making it very stable and difficult to remove electrons from. Carbon, nitrogen, and sulfur have varying levels of electron s in their outer shells. S ulfur has more loosely bound electrons than carbon or nitrogen, but still not as easy to remove as those in the first shell. However, the key here is the relative height of the peak. For an element where the peak for the lowest ionization energy electrons is three times higher than others, it suggests a high abundance of those specific electrons. Neon's configuration means all its electrons are tightly bound, so there wouldn't be such a dramatic difference. But if we consider the core electrons versus valence, sulfur has a higher number of valence electrons compared to the others listed. Actually, looking again, the condition described fits best with an element having a single type of low- energy electron dominate. That points toward sulfur, as it has more electrons in lower energy", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1926", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most useful measure would be job satisfaction. That's because it directly reflects how happy and content employees are with their work environment, which is a strong indicator of whether they'll stick around long term.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1934", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most common cause of cerebral palsy is a trauma at the time of birth, so option A. This can include complications during delivery such as oxygen deprivation or physical injuries to the baby's brain. While other factors like dural hemorrhages or genetic conditions may play a role in some cases, they are less common than birth-related issues.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1942", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Among primates, a high degree of sexual dimorph ism usually indicates intense competition between B. male s in order to obtain mates. This means that the physical differences between males and females are pronounced because males often compete aggressively for access to females during reproduct ive periods.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1950", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The fact that the moon always shows its same face to Earth is evidence that the moon rotates about its axis once per month. This phenomenon, known as synchronous rotation or tidal lock, means that the moon's rotational period matches its orbital period around Earth. So the correct answer is B, month.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1958", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 26, "onset_chunk": 25, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A web proxy is a piece of software that intercepts and possibly modifies request s and responses between a web browser and web server. It sits in the middle, listen ing to traffic going back and forth and can inspect or even change data as it passes through. This makes it useful for things like debugging network calls, monitor ing traffic, or applying security filter s before requests reach the actual server.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1966", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 23, "onset_chunk": 22, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. Decre ase the money supply, increase taxes, and reduce government spending all help to close an inflationary gap by reducing aggregate demand.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1974", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 25, "onset_chunk": 25, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A. The precedent established in Larry P v Riles resulted in the provision of a free, appropriate public education for students with disab ilities. This landmark case helped ensure that school s provide the necessary support and services to enable children with disabilities to receive an education tailored to their needs.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1982", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Clifford and Lucia Pauling, in their senior view, told us that physical changes take a long time.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1990", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In a series circuit, the current is the same throughout all components. So if one lamp has 2A of current, the next one will also have 2A. The correct answer is B, 2 A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
