{"id": "z2094", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 36, "onset_chunk": 35, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, why do scientists think that Mars was once warmer and wetter? Well, there's a lot of evidence for this. One of the main reasons is because we see lots of geological features on Mar s that are really hard to explain unless liquid water was stable at the surface. For example, there' s something called valley networks on Mars. These look just like river systems here on Earth, with channels and things branching off in different ways. And it's very hard to imagine how you'd get those kinds of patterns without water flow ing through them. Also, there' s evidence of ancient lake bed s. You can see flat areas that were probably lakes millions of years ago.And then even more recently, mission s like NASA's Cur iosity rover have found minerals that only form in the presence of water. So all these clues together— the valleys, the lake beds, the mineral s—point towards a time when Mars had a much warm er climate and liquid water on its surface.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 45, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2102", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A Gantt chart is a type of work schedule design. It visually represents tasks over time, showing start and end dates for each activity to help plan and track progress.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
