{"id": "z2198", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The fallacy that involves reasoning where you determine the conclusion you want first, then only accept evidence supporting it or interpret all evidence as support is called ad igno rantiam. So the correct answer is A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2206", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 21, "onset_chunk": 20, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "This is an example of unsupervis ed learning. In this case, we're given a large dataset of medical records without any explicit labels or target variables that tell us which patients belong to which clusters. Our goal is to discover hidden patterns or group s in the data based on the features present in the records. Since we are not using labeled examples to train a model, but rather finding natural groupings within the data itself, it falls under the category of unsupervised learning. The correct answer is B: Unsupervised learning.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2214", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, Mer rowe ther and William. Lewis was actually Mer rowe ther Lewis, and Clark was William Clark. These two explorers embarked on a historic journey across the American West in the early 1 800s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2222", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The rational decision-making model is based on a few key assumptions. One of them is that there's an agreed goal, so everyone knows what they're trying to achieve. Another assumption is that the problem is structured, meaning it can be clearly defined and broken down into steps. And another is that there is a high level of certainty regarding the environment— you have enough information to make informed choices. In complete information is actually not assumed because the model works best when all relevant data is available. So the answer is A: in complete information.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
